  "reference_no_of_permission_being_relied_on": "14/08099/LBC - Use of the listed Riding School as a private ancillary leisure facility and associated internal and external alterations.\n\n16/12269/LBC - Variation of approved drawings under 14/08099/LBC to allow adjustments to the configuration of the accommodation stairs and lifts at mezzanine, ground and lower ground floor levels, adjustment to the configuration of the lower ground floor adjustment to the design of the western pavilion, rearrangement of the internal configuration along with a repositioning of the connection point and retention and repair of the existing external brickwork.\n\n18/02330/LBC - Variation of approved drawings under 16/12269/LBC comprising: east elevation with agricultural doors added to the outside; Internal layout adjustments at lower ground, ground and first floor; further design development of the historic apertures and openings.\n\n18/09838/LBC - Variation of approved drawings under 18/02330/LBC comprising: amended roof eaves; development of capping beam; external brick repair/replacement work and east corbel detail/adjustment to the clock tower with creation of plant room and amendment to location of return air slot and provision of internal access to the rooflights for cleaning/maintenance purposes. And to wording of condition 8 in relation to limewash.\n\n",
